/* PATCH 329: the MGAVIDEO pitch-cache STATE words DGROUP:0x794 (current row-offset-table near offset)
 * and DGROUP:0x796 (current pitch) are 16-bit WORDs -- every asm access is a WORD:
 *   0x2c1: a3 96 07           mov ds:0x796,ax          (opcode A3 = mov moffs16,ax)
 *   0x2c9: c7 06 94 07 c8 07  mov WORD PTR ds:0x794,0x7c8
 *   0x2f1: a3 94 07           mov ds:0x794,ax
 * Ghidra typed BOTH `undefined4`, so `_DAT_1000_c796 = param_1` (asm 0x2c1) wrote FOUR bytes over
 * 0x796..0x799 and CLOBBERED word[DGROUP:0x798] -- the head of the 8-node pitch->rowtable MRU FREE LIST
 * that FUN_0000_0284 builds (patch 326) -- to 0 on the very first 02c1 call, and `_DAT_1000_c794 = 0x7c8`
 * (asm 0x2c9) then wrote over 0x796 (the pitch) as well.  With the free list destroyed, any request for a
 * non-320 pitch makes 02c1's walk terminate immediately at the HEAD CELL itself (cur = 0x798, its link
 * being 0), so the build path takes the head cell's `[bx+4]` = word[DGROUP:0x79c] = 0 as its rowtable
 * buffer and `rep stosw`s 200 words at DGROUP:0x0000 -- the deterministic DGROUP[0x000..0x18f] block-zero
 * patch 326 documents, which ZEROES the engine STRSEG word[DGROUP:0x70] (0x2d74 -> 0).  Patch 326 fixed
 * 0284's free-list node LINKS; this is the second root that then wiped the list the driver had just built.
 * The rest of the driver already treats both slots as WORDs (fist_mga.c 0x2d1e/0x2d33 mode-set init and
 * the 0x3095/0x3102 blit reads), so the undefined4 typing was internally inconsistent too. */
